  "report_sha256": "995476297ac2e99710b26b67d9ecc3e95963ab624e68282e7b5108da077999d3",
  "scope": "Two development residuals: current original 1160 and historical forcing control 1189 from its older seed. Two reversed repetitions per policy and case, twelve advances and one shared 32-state allowance per worker. Early saved-pair selection changes scheduling only and retains pending/known-forcing priority and both cofactor proof obligations. All eight workers close their targets; matched complete worker costs, separate authority/global/reference costs, disk sizes and repeated logical outcomes are preserved. The union retains all old rows and both policies including avoided ordinary probes. Independent cold replay forbids new pattern recognition and reference expansion, checks both branches and SAT model lifts, all 3203 reference nodes, all original coverage, exact next selection and idempotent deltas. Five new tests cover unacquired pairs, no new external probing, partial/cold resumption, fallback, forcing priority and budget rejection. No confidence interval, holdout estimate, peak-RAM claim, optimal acquisition or unrestricted SAT bound. Timings concern structural coverage, which can require more work than finding one SAT witness.",
